**Theorem (Anholcer, Cichacz, Milanič, 2015)**

Let G be arbitrary connected graph of order n ≥ 3. Then

\[
s_g(G)=
\begin{cases}
n+2 & \text{when } G \cong K_{1,3^{2q+1}-2} \text{ for some integer } q \ge 1 \\
n+1 & \text{when } n = 2 \ (\mathrm{mod}\ 4) \wedge G \not\cong K_{1,3^{2q+1}-2} \\
n & \text{otherwise}
\end{cases}
\]

Other results (Anholcer, Cichacz, 2015+): slightly weaker theorem for disconnected graphs, including the results for cyclic groups.

