Let $f(n,k)$f(n,k) denote the maximum number of edges in an $n$n-vertex ordered 3-uniform hypergraph avoiding the ordered tight-path configuration with parameter $k$k, and let $P^{(3)}_s$P s(3)​ be the ordered 3-uniform tight path on $s$s vertices. Define

$$a=\left\lfloor\frac{(k+1)^2}{4}\right\rfloor,$$a=⌊4(k+1)2​⌋,

and, equivalently,

$$b=\left\lfloor\frac{(s-1)^2}{4}\right\rfloor.$$b=⌊4(s−1)2​⌋.

Asymptotic extremal conjecture for ordered 3-uniform tight paths. The constructions described in the source are asymptotically optimal:

$$f(n,k)=\left(1-\frac{1}{a}+o(1)\right)\binom{n}{3}.$$f(n,k)=(1−a 1​+o(1))(3 n​).

Equivalently,

$$\mathrm{ex}_<(n,P^{(3)}_s)=\left(1-\frac{1}{b}+o(1)\right)\binom{n}{3}.$$ex<​(n,P s(3)​)=(1−b 1​+o(1))(3 n​).

The preceding constructions give the corresponding lower bounds, so the conjecture concerns matching asymptotic upper bounds for all relevant parameters.

